-- Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. ch. 51), section 2015(d)(1) to (3): the work requirements (snap2).
-- SOURCE: usc07-ch51.txt, a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text; nothing here is verified against it.
-- JUST TRUE: the text says yes. JUST FALSE: the text says no in its own words. NOTHING: the text does not say.
-- "Good cause" and "voluntarily quits" are the Secretary's to define and compliance is the State agency's to decide (paragraph (1)(D)), so they are inputs.

§ `Section 2015(d)(1)(A): who is ineligible for refusing or failing to work`

-- THE CONDUCT clauses (i) to (vi) look at. One record, because there are thirteen facts.
DECLARE `s 2015(d)(1)(A) conduct` HAS
    `refuses to register for employment at the time of application and every 12 months thereafter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `refuses to participate in an employment and training program to the extent required by the State agency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `refuses to accept an offer of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offer is at a site or plant not subject to a strike or lockout at the time of the refusal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the hourly wage offered, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the applicable Federal or State minimum hourly wage, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the hourly wage that would have governed had the Fair Labor Standards Act minimum rate applied, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `refuses to provide the State agency with sufficient information to determine employment status or job availability` IS A BOOLEAN
    `voluntarily quits a job` IS A BOOLEAN
    `voluntarily reduces work effort` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours worked per week after the reduction` IS A NUMBER
    `fails to comply with section 2029` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there was good cause` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

-- src:536 | (A) In general.—
-- src:537 | No physically and mentally fit individual over the age of 15 and under the age of 60 shall be eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program if the individual—
-- src:538 | (i) refuses, at the time of application and every 12 months thereafter, to register for employment in a manner prescribed by the Secretary;
-- src:539 | (ii) refuses without good cause to participate in an employment and training program established under paragraph (4), to the extent required by the State agency;
-- src:540 | (iii) refuses without good cause to accept an offer of employment, at a site or plant not subject to a strike or lockout at the time of the refusal, at a wage not less than the higher of—
-- src:541 | (I) the applicable Federal or State minimum wage; or
-- src:542 | (II) 80 percent of the wage that would have governed had the minimum hourly rate under section 6(a)(1) of the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938 (29 U.S.C. 206(a)(1)) been applicable to the offer of employment;
-- src:543 | (iv) refuses without good cause to provide a State agency with sufficient information to allow the State agency to determine the employment status or the job availability of the individual;
-- src:544 | (v) voluntarily and without good cause—
-- src:545 | (I) quits a job; or
-- src:546 | (II) reduces work effort and, after the reduction, the individual is working less than 30 hours per week; or
-- src:547 | (vi) fails to comply with section 2029 of this title.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(1)(A) (src:536-547)
GIVEN `the age of the individual in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the individual is physically and mentally fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual's conduct` IS A `s 2015(d)(1)(A) conduct`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(1)(A) the individual is ineligible to participate in the program` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence reaches only "No physically and mentally fit individual over the age of 15 and under the age of 60"
        IF NOT (`the individual is physically and mentally fit` AND `the age of the individual in years` GREATER THAN 15 AND `the age of the individual in years` LESS THAN 60) THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be eligible to participate ... if the individual" (reading (a): no clause (i) to (vi) is met)
        OTHERWISE `s 2015 helper: some answer in the list holds` (LIST `clause (i)`, `clause (ii)`, `clause (iii)`, `clause (iv)`, `clause (v)`, `clause (vi)`)
    WHERE
        `the conduct` MEANS `the individual's conduct`
        -- "without good cause": the Secretary decides the meaning (subparagraph (D)(i)), so the answer is NOTHING when no determination is supplied
        `without good cause` MEANS `s 2015 helper: the answer reversed` (`the conduct`'s `there was good cause`)
        `clause (i)` MEANS JUST (`the conduct`'s `refuses to register for employment at the time of application and every 12 months thereafter`)
        `clause (ii)` MEANS `s 2015 helper: both answers hold` (JUST (`the conduct`'s `refuses to participate in an employment and training program to the extent required by the State agency`)) `without good cause`
        `clause (iii)` MEANS `s 2015 helper: both answers hold` (JUST (`the conduct`'s `refuses to accept an offer of employment` AND `the conduct`'s `the offer is at a site or plant not subject to a strike or lockout at the time of the refusal` AND `the conduct`'s `the hourly wage offered, in dollars` AT LEAST `s 2015 helper: the higher of two numbers` (`the conduct`'s `the applicable Federal or State minimum hourly wage, in dollars`) (0.8 TIMES `the conduct`'s `the hourly wage that would have governed had the Fair Labor Standards Act minimum rate applied, in dollars`))) `without good cause`
        `clause (iv)` MEANS `s 2015 helper: both answers hold` (JUST (`the conduct`'s `refuses to provide the State agency with sufficient information to determine employment status or job availability`)) `without good cause`
        `clause (v)` MEANS `s 2015 helper: both answers hold` (JUST (`the conduct`'s `voluntarily quits a job` OR (`the conduct`'s `voluntarily reduces work effort` AND `the conduct`'s `hours worked per week after the reduction` LESS THAN 30))) `without good cause`
        `clause (vi)` MEANS JUST (`the conduct`'s `fails to comply with section 2029`)

§ `Section 2015(d)(1)(B) and (C): the household, and how long`

-- src:548 | (B) Household ineligibility.—
-- src:549 | If an individual who is the head of a household becomes ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program under subparagraph (A), the household shall, at the option of the State agency, become ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program for a period, determined by the State agency, that does not exceed the lesser of—
-- src:550 | (i) the duration of the ineligibility of the individual determined under subparagraph (C); or
-- src:551 | (ii) 180 days.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(1)(B) (src:548-551)
GIVEN `the individual is the head of a household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual became ineligible under subparagraph (A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the State agency has chosen to make the household ineligible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the duration of the individual's ineligibility under subparagraph (C), in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2015(d)(1)(B) the longest period of household ineligibility the State agency may determine, in days` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an individual who is the head of a household becomes ineligible ... under subparagraph (A), the household shall, at the option of the State agency"
        IF NOT `the individual is the head of a household` THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (`the individual became ineligible under subparagraph (A)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT `the State agency has chosen to make the household ineligible` THEN NOTHING
        -- "a period ... that does not exceed the lesser of (i) the duration of the ineligibility of the individual determined under subparagraph (C); or (ii) 180 days"
        OTHERWISE JUST (`s 2015 helper: the lesser of two numbers` `the duration of the individual's ineligibility under subparagraph (C), in days` 180)

-- src:548 | (B) Household ineligibility.—
-- src:549 | If an individual who is the head of a household becomes ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program under subparagraph (A), the household shall, at the option of the State agency, become ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program for a period, determined by the State agency, that does not exceed the lesser of—
-- src:550 | (i) the duration of the ineligibility of the individual determined under subparagraph (C); or
-- src:551 | (ii) 180 days.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(1)(B) (src:548-551)
GIVEN `the longest period the State agency may determine, in days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the period the State agency determined, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(1)(B) the period the State agency determined is allowed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the longest period the State agency may determine, in days`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST longest THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period, determined by the State agency, that does not exceed the lesser of"
        IF `the period the State agency determined, in days` GREATER THAN longest THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 2015(d)(1)(C) outcome` IS ONE OF
    `s 2015(d)(1)(C) remains ineligible until` HAS `the date` IS A DATE
    `s 2015(d)(1)(C) remains ineligible permanently`
    `s 2015(d)(1)(C) not covered`

-- src:553 | (i) First violation.—
-- src:554 | The first time that an individual becomes ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program under subparagraph (A), the individual shall remain ineligible until the later of—
-- src:555 | (I) the date the individual becomes eligible under subparagraph (A);
-- src:556 | (II) the date that is 1 month after the date the individual became ineligible; or
-- src:557 | (III) a date determined by the State agency that is not later than 3 months after the date the individual became ineligible.
-- src:558 | (ii) Second violation.—
-- src:559 | The second time that an individual becomes ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program under subparagraph (A), the individual shall remain ineligible until the later of—
-- src:560 | (I) the date the individual becomes eligible under subparagraph (A);
-- src:561 | (II) the date that is 3 months after the date the individual became ineligible; or
-- src:562 | (III) a date determined by the State agency that is not later than 6 months after the date the individual became ineligible.
-- src:563 | (iii) Third or subsequent violation.—
-- src:564 | The third or subsequent time that an individual becomes ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program under subparagraph (A), the individual shall remain ineligible until the later of—
-- src:565 | (I) the date the individual becomes eligible under subparagraph (A);
-- src:566 | (II) the date that is 6 months after the date the individual became ineligible;
-- src:567 | (III) a date determined by the State agency; or
-- src:568 | (IV) at the option of the State agency, permanently.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(1)(C) (src:553-568)
GIVEN `the number of the violation, counting from 1` IS A NUMBER
      `the date the individual became ineligible` IS A DATE
      `the date the individual becomes eligible under subparagraph (A), if it has come` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the State agency determined, if it determined one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the State agency has elected permanent ineligibility` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 2015(d)(1)(C) outcome`
`s 2015(d)(1)(C) the individual remains ineligible until` MEANS
    -- MONTH ARITHMETIC (fork F-mo, NOTES): "the date that is 1 month after, 3 months after or 6 months after the date the individual became ineligible" is computed with `add months`, which CLAMPS the day to the last day of a shorter month (31 January 2026 plus 1 month is 28 February 2026). The text does not say how a month is counted when the later month lacks the day; the other readings are "not covered" and rolling forward to 3 March.
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a violation numbered below the first is not described
        IF `the number of the violation, counting from 1` LESS THAN 1 THEN `s 2015(d)(1)(C) not covered`
        -- clause (iii)(IV): "at the option of the State agency, permanently" (third or subsequent violation only)
        IF `the number of the violation, counting from 1` AT LEAST 3 AND `the State agency has elected permanent ineligibility` THEN `s 2015(d)(1)(C) remains ineligible permanently`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the State agency's date is "not later than 3 months" (first violation) or "not later than 6 months" (second) after the date of ineligibility
        IF `the cap breached` THEN `s 2015(d)(1)(C) not covered`
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the "later of" cannot be fixed until the date in subclause (I) has come
        IF `the date the individual becomes eligible under subparagraph (A), if it has come` EQUALS NOTHING THEN `s 2015(d)(1)(C) not covered`
        OTHERWISE `s 2015(d)(1)(C) remains ineligible until` (`the later of the dates`)
    WHERE
        `the months in subclause (II)` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the number of the violation, counting from 1` EQUALS 1 THEN 1
                IF `the number of the violation, counting from 1` EQUALS 2 THEN 3
                OTHERWISE 6
        `the cap in months for subclause (III)` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the number of the violation, counting from 1` EQUALS 1 THEN JUST 3
                IF `the number of the violation, counting from 1` EQUALS 2 THEN JUST 6
                OTHERWISE NOTHING
        `the cap breached` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the date the State agency determined, if it determined one`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST d THEN
                CONSIDER `the cap in months for subclause (III)`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                WHEN JUST m THEN d GREATER THAN `add months` `the date the individual became ineligible` m
        `the later of the dates` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the date the individual becomes eligible under subparagraph (A), if it has come`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date the individual became ineligible`
            WHEN JUST e THEN
                CONSIDER `the date the State agency determined, if it determined one`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 2015 helper: the later of two dates` e (`add months` `the date the individual became ineligible` `the months in subclause (II)`)
                WHEN JUST d THEN `s 2015 helper: the later of two dates` d (`s 2015 helper: the later of two dates` e (`add months` `the date the individual became ineligible` `the months in subclause (II)`))

§ `Section 2015(d)(1)(D): administration`

-- src:570 | (i) Good cause.—
-- src:571 | The Secretary shall determine the meaning of good cause for the purpose of this paragraph.
-- src:572 | (ii) Voluntary quit.—
-- src:573 | The Secretary shall determine the meaning of voluntarily quitting and reducing work effort for the purpose of this paragraph.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(1)(D)(i) and (ii) (src:570-573)
GIVEN `the Secretary's meaning covers the reason` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(1)(D)(i) and (ii) there is good cause, or the individual voluntarily quit or reduced work effort, as the Secretary determines` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "The Secretary shall determine the meaning of good cause" and "of voluntarily quitting and reducing work effort"; with no determination supplied the answer is NOTHING
    `the Secretary's meaning covers the reason`

-- src:574 | (iii) Determination by state agency.—
-- src:575 | (I) In general.—
-- src:576 | Subject to subclause (II) and clauses (i) and (ii), a State agency shall determine—
-- src:577 | (aa) the meaning of any term used in subparagraph (A);
-- src:578 | (bb) the procedures for determining whether an individual is in compliance with a requirement under subparagraph (A); and
-- src:579 | (cc) whether an individual is in compliance with a requirement under subparagraph (A).
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(1)(D)(iii)(I) (src:574-579)
GIVEN `the State agency's determination of the meaning, the procedure, or compliance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(1)(D)(iii)(I) the State agency determines the meaning of a term, the procedure, or whether the individual is in compliance` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "a State agency shall determine— (aa) the meaning of any term used in subparagraph (A); (bb) the procedures ...; and (cc) whether an individual is in compliance"; the determination is an input
    `the State agency's determination of the meaning, the procedure, or compliance`

-- src:580 | (II) Not less restrictive.—
-- src:581 | A State agency may not use a meaning, procedure, or determination under subclause (I) that is less restrictive on individuals receiving benefits under this chapter than a comparable meaning, procedure, or determination under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.).
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(1)(D)(iii)(II) (src:580-581)
GIVEN `the meaning, procedure or determination is less restrictive on individuals receiving benefits than the comparable one under the State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(1)(D)(iii)(II) the State agency may use the meaning, procedure or determination` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A State agency may not use a meaning, procedure, or determination under subclause (I) that is less restrictive"
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): one that is not less restrictive
    IF `the meaning, procedure or determination is less restrictive on individuals receiving benefits than the comparable one under the State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:582 | (iv) Strike against the government.—
-- src:583 | For the purpose of subparagraph (A)(v), an employee of the Federal Government, a State, or a political subdivision of a State, who is dismissed for participating in a strike against the Federal Government, the State, or the political subdivision of the State shall be considered to have voluntarily quit without good cause.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(1)(D)(iv) (src:582-583)
GIVEN `the individual is an employee of the Federal Government, a State, or a political subdivision of a State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual was dismissed for participating in a strike against that employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(1)(D)(iv) the individual is considered to have voluntarily quit without good cause` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming reaches an employee dismissed "for participating in a strike against the Federal Government, the State, or the political subdivision of the State"
    IF `the individual is an employee of the Federal Government, a State, or a political subdivision of a State` AND `the individual was dismissed for participating in a strike against that employer` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:584 | (v) Selecting a head of household.—
-- src:585 | (I) In general.—
-- src:586 | For purposes of this paragraph, the State agency shall allow the household to select any adult parent of a child in the household as the head of the household if all adult household members making application under the supplemental nutrition assistance program agree to the selection.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(1)(D)(v)(I) (src:584-586)
GIVEN `the person is an adult parent of a child in the household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all adult household members making application agree to the selection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(1)(D)(v)(I) the State agency must allow the household to select the person as head of the household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any adult parent of a child in the household"
        IF NOT `the person is an adult parent of a child in the household` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if all adult household members making application under the supplemental nutrition assistance program agree to the selection" (reading (a): a failed "if")
        IF NOT `all adult household members making application agree to the selection` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:587 | (II) Time for making designation.—
-- src:588 | A household may designate the head of the household under subclause (I) each time the household is certified for participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program, but may not change the designation during a certification period unless there is a change in the composition of the household.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(1)(D)(v)(II) (src:587-588)
GIVEN `the household is being certified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household is within a certification period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a change in the composition of the household` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(1)(D)(v)(II) the household is barred from changing the designation of the head` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A household may designate the head of the household under subclause (I) each time the household is certified" (a grant, so no bar)
        IF `the household is being certified` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless there is a change in the composition of the household"
        IF `the household is within a certification period` AND `there is a change in the composition of the household` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- "but may not change the designation during a certification period"
        IF `the household is within a certification period` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a time that is neither certification nor within a certification period
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:589 | (vi) Change in head of household.—
-- src:590 | If the head of a household leaves the household during a period in which the household is ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program under subparagraph (B)—
-- src:591 | (I) the household shall, if otherwise eligible, become eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program; and
-- src:592 | (II) if the head of the household becomes the head of another household, the household that becomes headed by the individual shall become ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program for the remaining period of ineligibility.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(1)(D)(vi) (src:589-592)
GIVEN `the head of the household leaves it during a period of ineligibility under subparagraph (B)` IS A BOOLEAN
