GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(1)(D)(vi)(I) the household becomes eligible when the head leaves` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the clause reaches a head who leaves "during a period in which the household is ineligible ... under subparagraph (B)"
        IF NOT `the head of the household leaves it during a period of ineligibility under subparagraph (B)` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the household shall, if otherwise eligible, become eligible" (reading (a): a failed "if")
        IF NOT `the household is otherwise eligible` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:589 | (vi) Change in head of household.—
