§ `Section 2015(d)(2): exemptions`

-- src:593 | (2) A person who otherwise would be required to comply with the requirements of paragraph (1) of this subsection shall be exempt from such requirements if he or she is (A) currently subject to and complying with a work registration requirement under title IV of the Social Security Act, as amended (42 U.S.C. 602), or the Federal-State unemployment compensation system, in which case, failure by such person to comply with any work requirement to which such person is subject shall be the same as failure to comply with that requirement of paragraph (1); (B) a parent or other member of a household with responsibility for the care of a dependent child under age six or of an incapacitated person; (C) a bona fide student enrolled at least half time in any recognized school, training program, or institution of higher education (except that any such person enrolled in an institution of higher education shall be ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program unless he or she meets the requirements of subsection (e) of this section); (D) a regular participant in a drug addiction or alcoholic treatment and rehabilitation program; (E) employed a minimum of thirty hours per week or receiving weekly earnings which equal the minimum hourly rate under the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938, as amended (29 U.S.C. 206(a)(1)), multiplied by thirty hours; or (F) a person between the ages of sixteen and eighteen who is not a head of a household or who is attending school, or enrolled in an employment training program, on at least a half-time basis. A State that requested a waiver to lower the age specified in subparagraph (B) and had the waiver denied by the Secretary as of August 1, 1996, may, for a period of not more than 3 years, lower the age of a dependent child that qualifies a parent or other member of a household for an exemption under subparagraph (B) to between 1 and 6 years of age.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(A) (src:593-593)
GIVEN `the person is currently subject to and complying with a work registration requirement under title IV of the Social Security Act or the Federal-State unemployment compensation system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(2)(A) the person is exempt because subject to and complying with another work registration requirement` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be exempt ... if he or she is (A) currently subject to and complying with" (reading (a): a failed "if")
    JUST `the person is currently subject to and complying with a work registration requirement under title IV of the Social Security Act or the Federal-State unemployment compensation system`

-- src:593 | (2) A person who otherwise would be required to comply with the requirements of paragraph (1) of this subsection shall be exempt from such requirements if he or she is (A) currently subject to and complying with a work registration requirement under title IV of the Social Security Act, as amended (42 U.S.C. 602), or the Federal-State unemployment compensation system, in which case, failure by such person to comply with any work requirement to which such person is subject shall be the same as failure to comply with that requirement of paragraph (1); (B) a parent or other member of a household with responsibility for the care of a dependent child under age six or of an incapacitated person; (C) a bona fide student enrolled at least half time in any recognized school, training program, or institution of higher education (except that any such person enrolled in an institution of higher education shall be ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program unless he or she meets the requirements of subsection (e) of this section); (D) a regular participant in a drug addiction or alcoholic treatment and rehabilitation program; (E) employed a minimum of thirty hours per week or receiving weekly earnings which equal the minimum hourly rate under the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938, as amended (29 U.S.C. 206(a)(1)), multiplied by thirty hours; or (F) a person between the ages of sixteen and eighteen who is not a head of a household or who is attending school, or enrolled in an employment training program, on at least a half-time basis. A State that requested a waiver to lower the age specified in subparagraph (B) and had the waiver denied by the Secretary as of August 1, 1996, may, for a period of not more than 3 years, lower the age of a dependent child that qualifies a parent or other member of a household for an exemption under subparagraph (B) to between 1 and 6 years of age.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(A) (src:593-593)
GIVEN `the person is exempt under clause (A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person failed to comply with a work requirement to which the person is subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(2)(A) the failure is the same as failure to comply with paragraph (1)` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in which case, failure by such person to comply with any work requirement to which such person is subject shall be the same as failure to comply with that requirement of paragraph (1)"
    IF `the person is exempt under clause (A)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the person failed to comply with a work requirement to which the person is subject` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:593 | (2) A person who otherwise would be required to comply with the requirements of paragraph (1) of this subsection shall be exempt from such requirements if he or she is (A) currently subject to and complying with a work registration requirement under title IV of the Social Security Act, as amended (42 U.S.C. 602), or the Federal-State unemployment compensation system, in which case, failure by such person to comply with any work requirement to which such person is subject shall be the same as failure to comply with that requirement of paragraph (1); (B) a parent or other member of a household with responsibility for the care of a dependent child under age six or of an incapacitated person; (C) a bona fide student enrolled at least half time in any recognized school, training program, or institution of higher education (except that any such person enrolled in an institution of higher education shall be ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program unless he or she meets the requirements of subsection (e) of this section); (D) a regular participant in a drug addiction or alcoholic treatment and rehabilitation program; (E) employed a minimum of thirty hours per week or receiving weekly earnings which equal the minimum hourly rate under the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938, as amended (29 U.S.C. 206(a)(1)), multiplied by thirty hours; or (F) a person between the ages of sixteen and eighteen who is not a head of a household or who is attending school, or enrolled in an employment training program, on at least a half-time basis. A State that requested a waiver to lower the age specified in subparagraph (B) and had the waiver denied by the Secretary as of August 1, 1996, may, for a period of not more than 3 years, lower the age of a dependent child that qualifies a parent or other member of a household for an exemption under subparagraph (B) to between 1 and 6 years of age.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(B) (src:593-593)
GIVEN `the person is a parent or other member of a household with responsibility for the care of a dependent child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the age of that child in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the age below which a child is dependent for this clause, 6 unless the State lowered it` IS A NUMBER
      `the person has responsibility for the care of an incapacitated person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(2)(B) the person is exempt because of responsibility for the care of a dependent child or an incapacitated person` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be exempt ... if he or she is (A) ... (B) a parent or other member of a household with responsibility for the care of a dependent child under age six or of an incapacitated person" (reading (a): a failed "if")
    JUST ((`the person is a parent or other member of a household with responsibility for the care of a dependent child` AND `the age of that child in years` LESS THAN `the age below which a child is dependent for this clause, 6 unless the State lowered it`)
          OR `the person has responsibility for the care of an incapacitated person`)

-- src:593 | (2) A person who otherwise would be required to comply with the requirements of paragraph (1) of this subsection shall be exempt from such requirements if he or she is (A) currently subject to and complying with a work registration requirement under title IV of the Social Security Act, as amended (42 U.S.C. 602), or the Federal-State unemployment compensation system, in which case, failure by such person to comply with any work requirement to which such person is subject shall be the same as failure to comply with that requirement of paragraph (1); (B) a parent or other member of a household with responsibility for the care of a dependent child under age six or of an incapacitated person; (C) a bona fide student enrolled at least half time in any recognized school, training program, or institution of higher education (except that any such person enrolled in an institution of higher education shall be ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program unless he or she meets the requirements of subsection (e) of this section); (D) a regular participant in a drug addiction or alcoholic treatment and rehabilitation program; (E) employed a minimum of thirty hours per week or receiving weekly earnings which equal the minimum hourly rate under the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938, as amended (29 U.S.C. 206(a)(1)), multiplied by thirty hours; or (F) a person between the ages of sixteen and eighteen who is not a head of a household or who is attending school, or enrolled in an employment training program, on at least a half-time basis. A State that requested a waiver to lower the age specified in subparagraph (B) and had the waiver denied by the Secretary as of August 1, 1996, may, for a period of not more than 3 years, lower the age of a dependent child that qualifies a parent or other member of a household for an exemption under subparagraph (B) to between 1 and 6 years of age.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2) (src:593-593)
GIVEN `the State requested a waiver to lower the age specified in subparagraph (B) and had it denied by the Secretary as of August 1, 1996` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the years for which the State lowers the age` IS A NUMBER
      `the age to which the State lowers it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(2) the State may lower the age of the dependent child` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence reaches "A State that requested a waiver to lower the age specified in subparagraph (B) and had the waiver denied by the Secretary as of August 1, 1996"
        IF NOT `the State requested a waiver to lower the age specified in subparagraph (B) and had it denied by the Secretary as of August 1, 1996` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of not more than 3 years" and "to between 1 and 6 years of age"
        IF `the years for which the State lowers the age` GREATER THAN 3 THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the age to which the State lowers it` LESS THAN 1 OR `the age to which the State lowers it` AT LEAST 6 THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:593 | (2) A person who otherwise would be required to comply with the requirements of paragraph (1) of this subsection shall be exempt from such requirements if he or she is (A) currently subject to and complying with a work registration requirement under title IV of the Social Security Act, as amended (42 U.S.C. 602), or the Federal-State unemployment compensation system, in which case, failure by such person to comply with any work requirement to which such person is subject shall be the same as failure to comply with that requirement of paragraph (1); (B) a parent or other member of a household with responsibility for the care of a dependent child under age six or of an incapacitated person; (C) a bona fide student enrolled at least half time in any recognized school, training program, or institution of higher education (except that any such person enrolled in an institution of higher education shall be ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program unless he or she meets the requirements of subsection (e) of this section); (D) a regular participant in a drug addiction or alcoholic treatment and rehabilitation program; (E) employed a minimum of thirty hours per week or receiving weekly earnings which equal the minimum hourly rate under the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938, as amended (29 U.S.C. 206(a)(1)), multiplied by thirty hours; or (F) a person between the ages of sixteen and eighteen who is not a head of a household or who is attending school, or enrolled in an employment training program, on at least a half-time basis. A State that requested a waiver to lower the age specified in subparagraph (B) and had the waiver denied by the Secretary as of August 1, 1996, may, for a period of not more than 3 years, lower the age of a dependent child that qualifies a parent or other member of a household for an exemption under subparagraph (B) to between 1 and 6 years of age.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(C) (src:593-593)
GIVEN `the person is a bona fide student enrolled at least half time in a recognized school, training program, or institution of higher education` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is enrolled in an institution of higher education` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person meets the requirements of subsection (e)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(2)(C) the person is exempt because a bona fide student enrolled at least half time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be exempt ... if he or she is (A) ... (C) a bona fide student enrolled at least half time" (reading (a): a failed "if")
        IF NOT `the person is a bona fide student enrolled at least half time in a recognized school, training program, or institution of higher education` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF NOT `the person is enrolled in an institution of higher education` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- the parenthesis: a student in higher education "shall be ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program unless he or she meets the requirements of subsection (e)"
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be ineligible to participate ... unless he or she meets the requirements of subsection (e)"
        IF `the person meets the requirements of subsection (e)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE `the person meets the requirements of subsection (e)`

-- src:593 | (2) A person who otherwise would be required to comply with the requirements of paragraph (1) of this subsection shall be exempt from such requirements if he or she is (A) currently subject to and complying with a work registration requirement under title IV of the Social Security Act, as amended (42 U.S.C. 602), or the Federal-State unemployment compensation system, in which case, failure by such person to comply with any work requirement to which such person is subject shall be the same as failure to comply with that requirement of paragraph (1); (B) a parent or other member of a household with responsibility for the care of a dependent child under age six or of an incapacitated person; (C) a bona fide student enrolled at least half time in any recognized school, training program, or institution of higher education (except that any such person enrolled in an institution of higher education shall be ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program unless he or she meets the requirements of subsection (e) of this section); (D) a regular participant in a drug addiction or alcoholic treatment and rehabilitation program; (E) employed a minimum of thirty hours per week or receiving weekly earnings which equal the minimum hourly rate under the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938, as amended (29 U.S.C. 206(a)(1)), multiplied by thirty hours; or (F) a person between the ages of sixteen and eighteen who is not a head of a household or who is attending school, or enrolled in an employment training program, on at least a half-time basis. A State that requested a waiver to lower the age specified in subparagraph (B) and had the waiver denied by the Secretary as of August 1, 1996, may, for a period of not more than 3 years, lower the age of a dependent child that qualifies a parent or other member of a household for an exemption under subparagraph (B) to between 1 and 6 years of age.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(D) (src:593-593)
GIVEN `the person is a regular participant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2012(h) the program is a drug addiction or alcoholic treatment and rehabilitation program` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(2)(D) the person is exempt because a regular participant in a treatment and rehabilitation program` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be exempt ... if he or she is (A) ... (D) a regular participant" (reading (a): a failed "if")
        IF NOT `the person is a regular participant` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE `s 2012(h) the program is a drug addiction or alcoholic treatment and rehabilitation program`

-- src:593 | (2) A person who otherwise would be required to comply with the requirements of paragraph (1) of this subsection shall be exempt from such requirements if he or she is (A) currently subject to and complying with a work registration requirement under title IV of the Social Security Act, as amended (42 U.S.C. 602), or the Federal-State unemployment compensation system, in which case, failure by such person to comply with any work requirement to which such person is subject shall be the same as failure to comply with that requirement of paragraph (1); (B) a parent or other member of a household with responsibility for the care of a dependent child under age six or of an incapacitated person; (C) a bona fide student enrolled at least half time in any recognized school, training program, or institution of higher education (except that any such person enrolled in an institution of higher education shall be ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program unless he or she meets the requirements of subsection (e) of this section); (D) a regular participant in a drug addiction or alcoholic treatment and rehabilitation program; (E) employed a minimum of thirty hours per week or receiving weekly earnings which equal the minimum hourly rate under the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938, as amended (29 U.S.C. 206(a)(1)), multiplied by thirty hours; or (F) a person between the ages of sixteen and eighteen who is not a head of a household or who is attending school, or enrolled in an employment training program, on at least a half-time basis. A State that requested a waiver to lower the age specified in subparagraph (B) and had the waiver denied by the Secretary as of August 1, 1996, may, for a period of not more than 3 years, lower the age of a dependent child that qualifies a parent or other member of a household for an exemption under subparagraph (B) to between 1 and 6 years of age.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(E) (src:593-593)
GIVEN `hours worked per week` IS A NUMBER
      `weekly earnings in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the minimum hourly rate under the Fair Labor Standards Act, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(2)(E) the person is exempt because employed or earning at the minimum rate for thirty hours` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be exempt ... if he or she is (A) ... (E) employed a minimum of thirty hours per week or receiving weekly earnings which equal the minimum hourly rate ... multiplied by thirty hours" (reading (a): a failed "if")
    JUST (`hours worked per week` AT LEAST 30 OR `weekly earnings in dollars` AT LEAST `the minimum hourly rate under the Fair Labor Standards Act, in dollars` TIMES 30)

-- src:593 | (2) A person who otherwise would be required to comply with the requirements of paragraph (1) of this subsection shall be exempt from such requirements if he or she is (A) currently subject to and complying with a work registration requirement under title IV of the Social Security Act, as amended (42 U.S.C. 602), or the Federal-State unemployment compensation system, in which case, failure by such person to comply with any work requirement to which such person is subject shall be the same as failure to comply with that requirement of paragraph (1); (B) a parent or other member of a household with responsibility for the care of a dependent child under age six or of an incapacitated person; (C) a bona fide student enrolled at least half time in any recognized school, training program, or institution of higher education (except that any such person enrolled in an institution of higher education shall be ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program unless he or she meets the requirements of subsection (e) of this section); (D) a regular participant in a drug addiction or alcoholic treatment and rehabilitation program; (E) employed a minimum of thirty hours per week or receiving weekly earnings which equal the minimum hourly rate under the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938, as amended (29 U.S.C. 206(a)(1)), multiplied by thirty hours; or (F) a person between the ages of sixteen and eighteen who is not a head of a household or who is attending school, or enrolled in an employment training program, on at least a half-time basis. A State that requested a waiver to lower the age specified in subparagraph (B) and had the waiver denied by the Secretary as of August 1, 1996, may, for a period of not more than 3 years, lower the age of a dependent child that qualifies a parent or other member of a household for an exemption under subparagraph (B) to between 1 and 6 years of age.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(F) (src:593-593)
GIVEN `the age of the person in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the person is the head of a household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is attending school or enrolled in an employment training program on at least a half-time basis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(2)(F) the person is exempt because a person between sixteen and eighteen` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be exempt ... if he or she is (A) ... (F) a person between the ages of sixteen and eighteen who is not a head of a household or who is attending school" (reading (a): a failed "if"; "between" is read as including 16 and 18, see the fork register)
    JUST (`the age of the person in years` AT LEAST 16 AND `the age of the person in years` AT MOST 18
          AND ((NOT `the person is the head of a household`) OR `the person is attending school or enrolled in an employment training program on at least a half-time basis`))

-- src:593 | (2) A person who otherwise would be required to comply with the requirements of paragraph (1) of this subsection shall be exempt from such requirements if he or she is (A) currently subject to and complying with a work registration requirement under title IV of the Social Security Act, as amended (42 U.S.C. 602), or the Federal-State unemployment compensation system, in which case, failure by such person to comply with any work requirement to which such person is subject shall be the same as failure to comply with that requirement of paragraph (1); (B) a parent or other member of a household with responsibility for the care of a dependent child under age six or of an incapacitated person; (C) a bona fide student enrolled at least half time in any recognized school, training program, or institution of higher education (except that any such person enrolled in an institution of higher education shall be ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program unless he or she meets the requirements of subsection (e) of this section); (D) a regular participant in a drug addiction or alcoholic treatment and rehabilitation program; (E) employed a minimum of thirty hours per week or receiving weekly earnings which equal the minimum hourly rate under the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938, as amended (29 U.S.C. 206(a)(1)), multiplied by thirty hours; or (F) a person between the ages of sixteen and eighteen who is not a head of a household or who is attending school, or enrolled in an employment training program, on at least a half-time basis. A State that requested a waiver to lower the age specified in subparagraph (B) and had the waiver denied by the Secretary as of August 1, 1996, may, for a period of not more than 3 years, lower the age of a dependent child that qualifies a parent or other member of a household for an exemption under subparagraph (B) to between 1 and 6 years of age.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2) (src:593-593)
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, c IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, d IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, e IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, f IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(2) the person is exempt from the requirements of paragraph (1)` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be exempt ... if he or she is (A) ... (F)" (reading (a): none of the six limbs is met)
    `s 2015 helper: some answer in the list holds` (LIST a, b, c, d, e, f)

-- src:593 | (2) A person who otherwise would be required to comply with the requirements of paragraph (1) of this subsection shall be exempt from such requirements if he or she is (A) currently subject to and complying with a work registration requirement under title IV of the Social Security Act, as amended (42 U.S.C. 602), or the Federal-State unemployment compensation system, in which case, failure by such person to comply with any work requirement to which such person is subject shall be the same as failure to comply with that requirement of paragraph (1); (B) a parent or other member of a household with responsibility for the care of a dependent child under age six or of an incapacitated person; (C) a bona fide student enrolled at least half time in any recognized school, training program, or institution of higher education (except that any such person enrolled in an institution of higher education shall be ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program unless he or she meets the requirements of subsection (e) of this section); (D) a regular participant in a drug addiction or alcoholic treatment and rehabilitation program; (E) employed a minimum of thirty hours per week or receiving weekly earnings which equal the minimum hourly rate under the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938, as amended (29 U.S.C. 206(a)(1)), multiplied by thirty hours; or (F) a person between the ages of sixteen and eighteen who is not a head of a household or who is attending school, or enrolled in an employment training program, on at least a half-time basis. A State that requested a waiver to lower the age specified in subparagraph (B) and had the waiver denied by the Secretary as of August 1, 1996, may, for a period of not more than 3 years, lower the age of a dependent child that qualifies a parent or other member of a household for an exemption under subparagraph (B) to between 1 and 6 years of age.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2) (src:593-593)
GIVEN b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, c IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, d IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, e IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, f IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(2)(B) to (F) the person is exempt from section 2015(d)(1) as the result of clause (B), (C), (D), (E), or (F)` MEANS
    -- the form that section 2029(b)(1) cites: "exempt from section 2015(d)(1) of this title as the result of clause (B), (C), (D), (E), or (F) of section 2015(d)(2)"
    `s 2015 helper: some answer in the list holds` (LIST b, c, d, e, f)

§ `Section 2015(d)(3): strikes`

-- src:594 | (3) Notwithstanding any other provision of law, a household shall not participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program at any time that any member of such household, not exempt from the work registration requirements of paragraph (1) of this subsection, is on strike as defined in section 142(2) of title 29, because of a labor dispute (other than a lockout) as defined in section 152(9) of title 29: Provided, That a household shall not lose its eligibility to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program as a result of one of its members going on strike if the household was eligible immediately prior to such strike, however, such household shall not receive an increased allotment as the result of a decrease in the income of the striking member or members of the household: Provided further, That such ineligibility shall not apply to any household that does not contain a member on strike, if any of its members refuses to accept employment at a plant or site because of a strike or lockout.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(3) (src:594-594)
GIVEN `a member not exempt from the work registration requirements of paragraph (1) is on strike because of a labor dispute other than a lockout` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household was eligible immediately prior to the strike` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household contains no member on strike and a member refuses employment at a plant or site because of a strike or lockout` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(3) the household shall not participate while the member is on strike` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "such ineligibility shall not apply to any household that does not contain a member on strike, if any of its members refuses to accept employment at a plant or site because of a strike or lockout" (placed first: it speaks of a household with NO member on strike, so it must be reached before the not-on-strike branch below)
        IF `the household contains no member on strike and a member refuses employment at a plant or site because of a strike or lockout` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rule is for a household with "any member of such household, not exempt from the work registration requirements of paragraph (1) of this subsection, is on strike"
        IF NOT `a member not exempt from the work registration requirements of paragraph (1) is on strike because of a labor dispute other than a lockout` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a household shall not lose its eligibility ... as a result of one of its members going on strike if the household was eligible immediately prior to such strike"
        IF `the household was eligible immediately prior to the strike` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:594 | (3) Notwithstanding any other provision of law, a household shall not participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program at any time that any member of such household, not exempt from the work registration requirements of paragraph (1) of this subsection, is on strike as defined in section 142(2) of title 29, because of a labor dispute (other than a lockout) as defined in section 152(9) of title 29: Provided, That a household shall not lose its eligibility to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program as a result of one of its members going on strike if the household was eligible immediately prior to such strike, however, such household shall not receive an increased allotment as the result of a decrease in the income of the striking member or members of the household: Provided further, That such ineligibility shall not apply to any household that does not contain a member on strike, if any of its members refuses to accept employment at a plant or site because of a strike or lockout.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(3) (src:594-594)
GIVEN `the household was eligible immediately prior to the strike` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a member of the household is striking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the increase in the allotment is the result of a decrease in the income of the striking member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(3) the household may receive an increased allotment as the result of a decrease in the income of the striking member` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "such household shall not receive an increased allotment as the result of a decrease in the income of the striking member or members of the household"
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a household not eligible before the strike, or an increase with another cause
    IF `the household was eligible immediately prior to the strike` AND `a member of the household is striking` AND `the increase in the allotment is the result of a decrease in the income of the striking member` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING
